<attribute name="mainDescription" nodeId="895f392a">&lt;p&gt;
    The evaluation includes various aspects, such as the overall opinion of the course, the instructor&apos;s performance, the
    course&apos;s meeting of expectations, the effectiveness of materials and equipment, and the feedback on the learning
    organization. Participants are also asked to identify the best and least effective aspects of the course and provide
    suggestions for improvement.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    In the context of digital learning, data is also collected from the Learning Experience Platform (LXP). This includes
    engagement data, remarks on media, interactions on social and group collaboration boards, and the uptake of additional
    content.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
<attribute name="externalId" nodeId="7b50cb4b"></attribute>
<attribute name="keyConsiderations" nodeId="87b4fea1"></attribute>
<attribute name="longPresentationName" nodeId="806a0eba"></attribute>
<attribute name="purpose" nodeId="3ea9e43">&lt;p&gt;
    The purpose of the learning evaluation is to gather participant feedback to identify the achievement of learning
    objectives, the applicability of the learning to participant roles, and opportunities for program and content
    improvements. The evaluation aims to identify whether the learning objectives were achieved, assess the overall
    effectiveness and suitability of the the learning program and to gather suggestions for improvement. It is also used
    for obtaining feedback on the effectiveness of the instructor.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    By summarizing the raw data and reviewing the learning content with key stakeholders, necessary updates and workarounds
    can be identified to meet learning program objectives.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
